{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.domain`\n\nEach application domain defines what identifies a node across runs. Changes to a node's contents or outgoing edges preserve its identity.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has two testable obligations. First, a domain defines what identifies a node across runs, so the same identity must give the same node and path in a fresh domain instance. Second, changing a node's contents or outgoing edges must not change its identity.\n\n**Identity across runs**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[enum_node_ids_distinguish_requirements_and_source_items_in_one_domain]` asserts that a hierarchical requirement node gets the same `NodePath` in the original domain and in a fresh `ReviewDomain`. It also asserts that requirement and source identities differ, and that evidence stored under one identity is not found under another.\n- `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[habeas_paths_preserve_opaque_segments_and_separate_all_node_kinds]` covers every Habeas node kind. It asserts exact path segments, and that a domain rebuilt from a fresh `OutlineCache` gives an equal path. It also asserts that each field change gives a distinct path, so the identity includes all the fields it should.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_relationships_accept_opaque_types_and_send_only_errors]` asserts exact paths for the opaque `Identity` node data. It also asserts that different identities give different paths.\n- `src/authoring/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[domain_shares_discovery_snapshots_with_tracked_reads]` checks that a source node built from an address equals the node built from the selector, and checks its path.\n\n**Contents and edges do not change identity**\n- `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk]` edits a source file in two ways. First it adds an `{impl}` reference, which changes the subject's outgoing edges from none to one and changes the reference-set content. Then it changes the function body.\n  - After the first edit, the subject's `Implements` edge resolves to a node equal to the one built from the same selector. The retained `Record` still resolves its dependencies against the new domain, and `is_current` reports the record as no longer current.\n  - After the second edit, the node data of the original source node is re-interned in a new domain. It resolves to content with a different fingerprint, so the same identity now has different content.\n- The same edit-then-reread pattern appears in `domain_shares_discovery_snapshots_with_tracked_reads`.\n- `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk]` does not assert subject-path equality across the edge edit. Node identity here is the node data itself, so re-interning the same data gives the same node, which the test relies on. I judge this adequate.\n\nThe tests also cover the cited `requirements.sdk.domain` context: they exercise the domain trait members, including `node_path`, `node_content`, `outgoing_edges` and the evidence storage methods. I found no unmarked relevant tests and no missing scenarios.",
  "references": "78521c46b3d7e947f2b1c262b4ddec789e08bce27062b8e4b6647057a600a11c",
